# Map - Project Resume Point

This file is the AI agent's memory for the Map project. It is read first at session
start and updated at the end of every substantive session. It follows the completeness
rule (see `standards-meta.mdc`): record decisions, the reasoning behind them, what was
deferred and why, and what the agent got wrong - not just conclusions.

## Project Overview

Map is a C++17 project whose deliverable is a **single static library, `Map.lib`**
(`libMap.a` on GCC/Clang/AppleClang). It provides the map model layer built on top
of the RMAP framework: the model objects **RMRoot / RMCObject / RMTObject / RMPObject**,
each with SB and IO source variants and factories, plus SB and IO package plugins, and a
`LibraryMVRP_Map` plugin that registers all the factories. The build is cross-platform
and **CMake is the single source of truth** (no committed IDE project files - they are
generated).

Naming note: the CMake project, target, deliverable, and package are all named **`Map`**
(`Map.sln`, `Map.vcxproj`, `Map.lib`, `find_package(Map)` -> `Map::Map`), fully symmetric
with RMAP (repo folder name == everything). The legacy MSVC project was named `MVRP_Map`
(`TargetName MVRP_Map`, `RootNamespace MVRPMapcpp`); that build-level name was dropped in
favor of `Map` at DavidSr's request. The C++ SOURCE identifiers and header file names are
still `MVRP_Map` (`include/MVRP_Map.h`, `MV_MVRP_MAP_API`, `LibraryMVRP_Map`) - those are
source, left to the pending migration, NOT changed by the build rename.

Located at `C:\Dev\OMB\Map`. Sibling projects under `C:\Dev\OMB`: `RMAP` (the converted
framework Map depends on), plus `Artemis`, `Sneeze`, `SneezeDoc`, `SneezeSDK`,
`SneezeSDK_C`, `SneezeSDK_CPP`, `SneezeSDK_Rust`.

